# Batch5 Native Screenshot Observation

Verdict: BLOCKED. Actual image opens: 8, each assigned PNG opened once using
`functions.view_image`; no reopens or crops. Seven image observations PASS;
`390-choices-0012.png` is BLOCKED for five unknown exercise 7 option tails.
All eight SHA-256 values were computed from the assigned PNG bytes and match
the selection manifest.

Scope is visible typography and display only. No browser, recapture, source,
answers, mathematical solving, choice correctness or figure semantic review.
PASS applies only to the displayed slice. Missing left prefixes, offscreen
headings and vertically neighboring content are complementary-limit. They do
not supply hidden text or resolve an unknown right terminal.

Snippets below are pixel transcriptions in ASCII: `^` denotes a visible
superscript, `/` a stacked fraction, `*` a visible multiplication dot, `!=` the
visible not-equal glyph and `sqrt(...)` a radical. These are not computed forms.
Image paths and hashes are bound individually in `result.json`.

